From: Christopher Owen <3221756+christopherowen@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 26 Oct 2026 17:29:12 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] [DS4.1] Attention front in one launch: q/kv norms, the
 Q-B cast, the kv RoPE and SWA record

attention_front is one kernel after the fused Q-A/KV projection in place of
five: TileKernels' RMSNorm of each latent, per_token_cast of the q latent,
rope_kernel on the kv latent and cache_writer_kernel's SWA record. q CTAs run a
TileLang port of TileKernels' norm_forward_and_per_token_cast (its row split,
fragment layouts, reducers and cast helpers); kv CTAs run the same norm, then
the RoPE and the record from registers, with those kernels' arithmetic.

Test: every output byte against the five kernels (BF16 q latent, E4M3 values,
UE8M0 scales, rotated kv latent, cache pages) at 1 to 65 rows, int64 and int32
slots, a skipped slot, and zero, large and tiny rows.
